# W10D1 - LangGraph Stateful Agent Graphs

## Overview

This project implements a three-node stateful agent graph using LangGraph.

The graph classifies user input, pauses for human review, and conditionally generates a response.

## Learning Objectives

- Build a stateful graph using LangGraph.
- Create three nodes: classify, route, and respond.
- Implement conditional edges.
- Use human-in-the-loop interrupts.
- Resume graph execution using Command(resume=...).
- Test classification and routing with five inputs.

## Architecture

START -> CLASSIFY -> ROUTE -> CONDITIONAL ROUTING

Conditional outcomes:

- Approved and safe -> RESPOND -> END
- Rejected -> END
- Unsafe -> END

## Technologies

- Python
- LangGraph
- pytest

## Project Structure

